# 30. Performance Bottleneck Diagnostic

The national performance system should eventually ask, for each major conservation objective:

| Question                                     | If "No"               | Likely bottleneck |
| -------------------------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------- |
| Do we know the condition?                    | Information absent    | Knowledge         |
| Do we understand the cause?                  | Diagnosis incomplete  | Diagnosis         |
| Can someone act?                             | Authority absent      | Authority         |
| Are resources available?                     | Funding inadequate    | Allocation        |
| Can institutions implement?                  | Capacity inadequate   | Capacity          |
| Are relevant actors connected?               | Fragmentation         | Coordination      |
| Is the intervention ecologically sufficient? | Biological constraint | Ecological        |
| Can gains be maintained?                     | Follow-up inadequate  | Durability        |

This transforms performance reporting from a passive reporting exercise into a diagnostic tool.

